A1. The girls they left behind them. ~ SPINSTERS
A9. This is always well protected by locks. ~ SCALP
A14. This one is not high toned. ~ ALTO
A15. You will find a mix-up here. ~ OLIO
A16. This is rare and also well done. ~ CURIO
A17. A general they called "Massa Bob". ~ LEE
A18. A place where you give dollars for quarters. ~ INN
A19. These are plane on the surface. ~ AREAS
A20. You will find one of these in every scenario. ~ VAMP
A22. This is what a cool summer can do. ~ ADD
A23. A lonely figure. ~ ONE
A24. This always stands for the right. ~ RT
A25. A flowery extract. ~ ESSENCE
A27. Achieved. ~ DID
A28. This is adorable. ~ PET
A29. A raw deal from the chef. ~ SALAD
A31. This one has always been on the staff. ~ FA
A32. This is what the ambitious young man will do for his education. ~ OWE
A35. This is often followed by a series. ~ WORLD
A37. A restful day in September. ~ LABOR
A39. This is what a calf will do to a silk sock. ~ FILL
A41. These are the ways that lead to the wicked city. ~ ROADS
A43. A sprinter's measure. ~ YARD
A44. This is what you will have to be in order to keep up. ~ FLIER
A46. The long and short of this is continually changing. ~ STYLE
A48. Signs of the times. ~ ADS
A49. A part of Italy. ~ IT
A50. You might get a laugh out of this. ~ TEHEE
A52. This runs free up in Canada. ~ ELK
A54. This keeps the traffic moving. ~ GAS
A55. Chooses. ~ SELECTS
A59. A French connection. ~ ET
A61. What some people are apt to throw when they get angry. ~ FIT
A62. This goes around after office hours. ~ MOP
A63. What a red hot poker will do. ~ GLOW
A64. This will help you down that long, long trail. ~ BURRO
A66. This won't get you very far in Paris. ~ SOU
A67. Before. ~ ERE
A68. This was strong on the market today. ~ ONION
A69. This is very grasping. ~ HAND
A71. A kitchen cleanser. ~ MAID
A72. These like to play a safe game. ~ YEGGS
A73. This has been put to flight. ~ ENDURANCE

D1. This is used to smooth down. ~ SALVE
D2. Entreaties. ~ PLEAS
D3. They always add these on hotel bills. ~ ITEMS
D4. This will deny anything. ~ NO
D5. This always comes before day. ~ TO
D6. To cut out. ~ ELIDE
D7. This is never the whole cheese. ~ RIND
D8. Heir-male. ~ SON
D9. A piece of this dished up with the coffee makes an enjoyable dinner. ~ SCANDAL
D10. What "Judge" will do for the blues. ~ CURE
D11. To be is in a different mood today. ~ ARE
D12. This is hard to believe. ~ LIAR
D13. Scotch stationery. ~ POSTCARDS
D21. Something a jelly-fish lacks. ~ PEP
D22. This fellow's work is all play. ~ ACTOR
D23. This one is always gushing over the beautiful country. ~ OIL
D26. This is rather fresh. ~ NEW
D27. A gold-digger's tool. ~ DADDY
D29. Where the older generation used to solve their problems. ~ SLATE
D30. This is what always comes after a restless night. ~ DAY
D31. This man develops plants and always gets a bumper crop. ~ FORD
D32. The relations of this one, in connection with the ball games, are fast expiring. ~ OFFICEBOY
D33. What a modest violet will do. ~ WILT
D34. Only one term at Yale. ~ ELI
